Hi, the parametrization would be:

alpha=r=shape (indeed)

and

mu = alpha/beta -> beta = alpha/mu

In your code (workaround) you use:

             y_rep [i] <- poisson_rng (gamma_rng (shape,
                 shape / mu_rep [i]));

which means
             y_rep [i] <- poisson_rng (gamma_rng (alpha,
                 beta));

If your code is correct, than stan's isn't:

     neg_binomial_rng(const double alpha,
                      const double beta,
                      RNG& rng) {
      (...)

       return stan::prob::poisson_rng(stan::prob::gamma_rng(alpha, 1.0 /
beta,
rng),rng);

     }

