Anything that cuts down on gradient times is worth
exploring.

There's not a good way to write that within Stan as of
now, because we don't have any associative array types that
would let us do the aggregation in a general way.  But we
could perhaps build a special function to do the aggregation
(also difficult because we don't have structured return values
and here you want vectors paired with counts).  Or we could
build something like this into the vectorization.

A simple example would be converting a vectorized bernoulli
into a binomial, so that if y is an int array, then

  y ~ bernoulli(theta);

would essentially get evaluated as

  sum(y) ~ binomial(size(y), theta);

- Bob

