> In the data saved as KWDYZ_test.rda and provided by Shravan in a December posting on "lmer versus stan" the vector of responses and the number of rows in the model matrices is 28710.  However, in the model matrix for the fixed-effects parameters there are only 4 distinct rows.  For the random effects there are 244 distinct combinations of id, c1, c2 and c3.
>
> It occurs to me that there may be considerable savings in collapsing information in the model matrices to the unique rows and having an index vector to associate the rows of the collapsed model matrix with the observations.  It is not difficult to do the collasping in R
>
> > mm <- model.matrix(rt ~ c1 + c2 + c3, dat)
