Dear all,

I use the Negative Binomial to model distribution of counts. The way the NegBin is formulated in RStan isn't realy the same as in Wikipedia  <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Negative_binomial_distribution>... and I'm not strong enough to handle such troubles :-).
I modelled as follow:

Count[i] ~ NegBin( N[i], 1/f)

where N[i] is the size of the sample ; and "f" is the frequency of occurence of the success.
But as you write an " \alpha -1" in the definition of the density function, should I write: "Count[i] ~ NegBin( N[i]+1, 1/mu)"?

Thank you

